x, TTM) shown at 20% for Q1'26, 25% for Q4'26 and 25% for Q1'27, described as ▲+5.0 pp YoY.","src":"deck","title":"Capital allocation policy (investor deck)"}],"business":[{"body":"- \"Orbit Exports is a manufacturer and exporter of value-added fabrics, producing fancy jacquards, novelty and fashion fabrics alongside home-textile and finished made-up.\"\n- Serves apparel, home-furnishing and occasion-specific fabric markets across the US, Europe, the Middle East, Latin America, Africa and Southeast Asia, \"working with leading retailers and brands worldwide\" — i.e. an export-led customer base rather than a domestic one.\n- Reports on a consolidated basis under two segments per Ind AS 108 — Textile Business and Investments — with Investments disclosed as a separate reportable segment alongside the core textile operation.","src":"deck","title":"Positioning (investor deck)"},{"body":"- [Trade policy] \"The recent easing of tariffs by the United States has had a positive impact on Indian textile exporters, improving cost competitiveness and order visibility as compared to the same period last year.\"\n- [Trade policy] The India–UK Free Trade Agreement \"is expected to be a long-term positive for the industry, gradually opening up preferential access to a large export market, although its full benefit will be realised only over the coming years as trade flows adjust.\"\n- [Geopolitical risk] \"The ongoing Middle East crisis continues to weigh on global logistics, keeping shipping costs elevated and disrupting established trade routes; as a result, overall business volumes to the region for the quarter remain volatile.\"\n- [Segment mix] Total income by segment for Q1 FY26-27: Textile Business ₹7,819.13 Lakhs (88.9%) and Investments ₹972.33 Lakhs (11.1%); the deck notes the Textile Business result includes share of profit of associate and \"may differ from standalone figures presented elsewhere in this presentation\".\n- [Segment assets] The segment-assets chart carries 